# Footer anatomy (any landing)

When the design has a dark “stay connected / newsletter CTA” band above link columns, that whole block is usually the **Footer**, not a mid-page section.

FORJD example name: **Stay Connected**. Other brands may label it differently. Map by structure, not by title.

## Order (top → bottom)

1. **CTA band** (Stay Connected / Fuel A Brighter Tomorrow) + newsletter form + perk icons + script
2. **Main columns**: logo/tagline/social · Shop · Learn · Customer Care · Make an Impact
3. **Local Impact** (optional): map + state directory + store CTA
4. **Legal bar**: tagline · privacy/terms · copyright

## Pairing (map by role)

| Role in design | Typical component |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-page newsletter (“Stay in the Loop”, etc.) | `components/<landing>/Newsletter.tsx` or `home/Newsletter.tsx` |
| Footer CTA + link columns (+ local/legal) | `layout/Footer.tsx` |

Page order: `… → Newsletter → Footer`.

## Assets

- CTA bg: `cta-mountain-background` (or pack equivalent)
- Footer rock / map: footer pack paths in `brand.footer`
- Social: `social-*` light SVGs in circular hit targets

## Forms

Reuse shared `NewsletterForm` (react-hook-form). Do not duplicate uncontrolled inputs.
